## 2. `src/Collect.gs` — start marker

### 2.1 Placement

Immediately after the two prunes, before `deletePoolMojibake_`:

```js
var health = blankHealth_('collect', now);
try {
  prunePool_(now);
  pruneSeen_(now);
  writeHealth_(blankHealth_('collect-start', now));   // survives a timeout; see §2.3
  var nMojibake = deletePoolMojibake_();
  …
```

**A separate `blankHealth_` call, not the `health` object.** `health` accumulates counters and is written once at the end. Writing it twice would either emit a half-populated duplicate of the real row or require mutating and re-appending, which `writeHealth_` does not support.

**After the prunes, not before.** A start marker that precedes `prunePool_` would claim the execution reached `fetchFeeds` when it may have died in the prune. The prunes are also a plausible timeout site given pool size, so bracketing them is the point.

### 2.2 `kind` value

Use the literal `'collect-start'`. Read `blankHealth_` before writing this — confirm that a row built with an unfamiliar `kind` renders with the numeric columns blank or zero rather than throwing, and that `writeHealth_` does not validate `kind` against an allow-list. If it does validate, extend the allow-list; do not reuse `'collect'`, which would make start rows and completion rows indistinguishable and break the pairing in §4.

### 2.3 What this buys

| Health tab shows | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `collect-start` then `collect`, same hour | Normal execution |
| `collect-start`, no matching `collect` | **Timeout** (or an uncaught kill), timestamped to the minute it started |
| Neither row | Trigger did not fire, or `tryLock` returned early (console-only, by design) |

Those three were previously one indistinguishable symptom. The lock-skip branch stays console-only per `fix-spec-encoding-and-keys.md` §3 — do not add a health row there. A lock skip is not a collect, and it is now distinguishable anyway: it produces neither row, while a timeout produces the first.

### 2.4 Cost

24 extra `health` rows per day, one `appendRow` each (~0.5–1 s inside a 360 s budget). Nothing prunes the `health` tab today, so this roughly doubles its growth rate. Accepted for now; a `pruneHealth_` is a separate, later change and is **not** in scope here. Do not add one, and do not add a script property to gate the marker.

