## 3. `src/Collect.gs` — phase timing

### 3.1 Instrument three phases

Wall-clock brackets only. No profiler, no per-feed timing.

```js
var tFetch = Date.now();
var fetched = fetchFeeds(FEEDS);
var msFetch = Date.now() - tFetch;
console.log('collect ms fetch=' + msFetch);
```

```js
var tDedup = Date.now();
// …existing parse loop, loadPool/loadSeen, gap detection, survivor loop, unchanged…
var msDedup = Date.now() - tDedup;
console.log('collect ms dedup=' + msDedup);
```

```js
var tAppend = Date.now();
appendPool_(survivors, now);
health.poolSize = poolRowCount_();
var msAppend = Date.now() - tAppend;
console.log('collect ms append=' + msAppend);
```

Then extend the existing `notes` assembly — do not replace it:

```js
var notes = [];
if (nMojibake) notes.push('dropped mojibake: ' + nMojibake);
if (droppedDates) notes.push('dropped dateless: ' + droppedDates);
notes.push('ms fetch/dedup/append: ' + msFetch + '/' + msDedup + '/' + msAppend);
if (notes.length) health.notes = notes.join('; ');
```

`notes` is assembled before `appendPool_` in the current code. Move the `notes.push` for timings and the `health.notes` assignment to **after** the append block so `msAppend` exists. Leave the two existing `notes.push` calls where they are; only the join and assignment move.

### 3.2 Both channels, deliberately

The `console.log` lines survive a timeout in the editor Execution log for manual runs, and will survive one in Cloud Logging once GCP is attached. The `health.notes` string only lands on completed runs, but it is readable on the Sheet without opening anything else, and it accumulates a baseline. When a timeout does occur, the neighbouring completed rows show what the phase costs were at that pool size, which is the comparison that identifies the culprit.

### 3.3 The hypothesis being tested

`fetchFeeds` is a single `UrlFetchApp.fetchAll` and is unlikely to be the cost. The candidates are `deletePoolMojibake_` (row-by-row deletion), `prunePool_`, and the survivor loop, which runs trigram Dice for every parsed item against `sameDayPoolTitles_` — a set that grows through the day. That last one degrades with pool size, which fits timeouts clustering rather than appearing at random. `msDedup` covers the survivor loop; `deletePoolMojibake_` and the prunes fall outside all three brackets by design, so if `msFetch + msDedup + msAppend` is far short of the elapsed execution time shown in the Executions sidebar, the cost is in the unbracketed prefix and that is the next thing to bracket. Do not pre-emptively bracket it now — one round of data first.

**Do not change any dedup, prune, or mojibake logic in this spec.** Measure first. `LIMITS.titleSimilarity` stays 0.82 and `src/Config.gs` is not edited.

